\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Throughput comparison across confidential computing configurations. GPU baseline (123.5\nobreakspace  {}tok/s) drops by only 7\% with NVIDIA CC and 8\% with full governance. CPU TDX decode operates at lower absolute throughput but with only 2.1--5.2\% CC overhead. The $<$8\% bracket highlights that confidential+governed GPU inference remains within acceptable production overhead.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:throughput}{{5}{8}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Per-tenant cost comparison. Multi-tenant sharing with confidential computing achieves 4$\times $ savings (GPU: \$6.16 $\rightarrow $ \$1.54/tenant) and 6$\times $ savings (CPU TDX: \$4.20 $\rightarrow $ \$1.05/tenant). Orange line shows throughput overhead remains below 15\%. Net effect: 75\% cost reduction per tenant with full security hardening.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tco}{{6}{8}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Waterfall analysis of cumulative throughput impact per security hardening layer (H100 SXM, Llama-3.1-70B). TEE memory encryption ($-4.1\%$) and GPU CC mode ($-2.8\%$) dominate overhead. Governance ($-1.1\%$), bias monitoring ($-0.6\%$), and audit logging ($-0.4\%$) contribute minimal impact. Total: 15.8\% from 123.5 to 104.0\nobreakspace  {}tok/s for a fully hardened, governed, multi-tenant deployment.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{7}{8}}
